  "id": "COMPOUND:21489 - PROTEIN:5781",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Npc13565 and A2780cisR through a series of target interactions. Npc13565 is implicated in targeting SNU-387, which is a target of multiple compounds, including Neridienone A, 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, and sec-Butyl acetate, (-). All of these compounds are known to interact with A2780cisR, indicating a common downstream effect on this cell line. The cumulative scores from the three paths suggest a plausible mechanistic link, though the exact mode of action remains unclear. The evidence supports a pathway where Npc13565 may influence SNU-387, which in turn affects A2780cisR through multiple molecular mechanisms. The integration of these targets highlights the potential for Npc13565 to modulate A2780cisR via a complex network of interactions, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the specific mechanism.",
